<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — background-imagery dialog (Avalonia view), FEATURE-GATED.

    Parity SHELL of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormMap` (FormMap.cs + FormMap.Designer.cs, 422 lines).
    Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a 1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the current Windows Forms look,
    never a redesign: same window, same right-hand command panel, same control arrangement, same
    fonts. The operator originally used this dialog to pull online satellite imagery in behind the
    field and (optionally) trace a boundary over it.

    FEATURE-GATE (AAP §0.5.1 / §0.6.3 — F-021 "Replace or feature-gate"):
      The WinForms FormMap was built entirely on a Windows-only / abandoned online-imagery control and
      a Windows-only imaging stack (both removed types are named in MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md).
      Those are out of the cross-platform path and are REMOVED. This markup intentionally contains NO
      reference to any online-imagery type, NO Windows-only imaging type and NO online-imagery provider
      name — it is pure Avalonia. For first release the imagery feature is
      gated OFF: the large map surface (the WinForms `gMapControl`) is replaced by `mapPlaceholder`,
      a dark panel carrying a graceful "Background imagery unavailable on this platform" message — the
      established no-op graceful-degradation pattern (the field still renders fine without imagery and
      the cross-platform SQLite tile cache is unaffected elsewhere). The dialog still OPENS and shows
      its full control shell; it must NEVER throw and NEVER break startup. Because every operational
      control depends on the (now absent) imagery, they are shown but DISABLED (IsEnabled="False");
      only `btnExit` stays enabled so the dialog can always be closed.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormMap.Designer.cs:
      Text (online-imagery caption)    : Title. The runtime text is assigned by the code-behind to
                                          gStr.gsMapForBackground; the DESIGN-TIME literal here is kept
                                          deliberately provider-neutral ("Add Map as Background") to
                                          honour the "no online-imagery-provider references in this
                                          file" rule — the localised string lives in the frozen
                                          translation resources, not in this markup.
      ClientSize 1130 x 780            : Width / Height (initial client size; resizable).
      MinimumSize 1016 x 753           : MinWidth / MinHeight.
      FormBorderStyle (Sizable) + anchors : CanResize="True" (the map surface fills and the 241-wide
                                          command panel stays pinned to the right on resize, exactly
                                          reproducing the WinForms Anchor layout).
      ControlBox/Maximize/Minimize = false : the borderless title-bar-button toggles have no direct
                                          Avalonia equivalent; CanResize="True" preserves the resize
                                          behaviour that the WinForms MinimumSize + anchors implied.
      ShowInTaskbar = false            : ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition (CenterParent intent) : WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown owned/modal over
                                          FormGPS, per the AAP Avalonia wiring; this replaces the
                                          WinForms ScreenHelper on-screen reposition).
      BackColor WhiteSmoke             : Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}" — per this file's
                                          spec the neutral chrome is themed to the App.axaml day/night
                                          palette (the only dependency of this file) rather than
                                          hard-coding a WinForms colour.
      Font Tahoma                      : FontFamily="Tahoma"; children carry their point sizes converted
                                          to Avalonia device-independent pixels (pt × 96/72):
                                          14.25pt -> 19, 15.75pt -> 21.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind (FormMapView.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour:
      * This view is IMPERATIVE, not MVVM — there is intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext and
        NO {Binding}, exactly like the sibling code-behind dialogs (FormWebCamView / FormPanView /
        FormFieldDirView). The x:Name'd controls below are the entire integration surface and keep
        their ORIGINAL WinForms names so the migrated code-behind addresses them exactly as
        FormMap.cs did.
      * No Click= / event attributes are declared here on purpose: the handler method names are owned
        by the code-behind (which subscribes via the named fields, e.g. btnExit.Click += ...), so this
        markup never depends on a specific handler-method name (the FormWebCamView / FormPanView
        convention). The original FormMap_Load / btnExit_Click / btn*_Click / cbox*_Click /
        timer1_Tick logic is reproduced there.
      * Control-name contract (MUST stay spelled exactly): mapPlaceholder, btnZoomIn, btnZoomOut,
        btnAddFence, btnDeletePoint, btnDeleteAll, btnGo, btnExit, cboxDrawMap, cboxEnableLineDraw,
        labelBackground, labelBoundary, labelNewBoundary, lblBnds, lblPoints. (The WinForms designer
        had no find/search TextBox, so none is added.)
      * Design-time label texts below ("New Bnd", "Points: 12", "Boundary", "2", "Background") are the
        WinForms designer placeholders; at runtime the code-behind localises them via gStr
        (gsNewFromDefault+gsBoundary / gsPoints / gsBoundary / computed / gsBackground), mirroring
        FormMap.cs and the once-per-second timer1_Tick.

    Button / toggle glyphs are served from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares://
    URIs — the same btnImages/ assets every other GPS Avalonia view consumes, and the exact images the
    WinForms designer used (ZoomOGL / ZoomOut / AddNew / PointDelete / Trash / FlagGrn / OK64 /
    BoundaryOuter / MappingOff). No WinForms, no GL-host, no online-imagery, and no other Windows-only
    UI-toolkit types are referenced — pure Avalonia 11.3.x.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormMapView"
        Title="Add Map as Background"
        Width="1130"
        Height="780"
        MinWidth="1016"
        MinHeight="753"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="19"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <!--
        Shared control styles.

        Button.flatImage — the cross-platform equivalent of the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor = Transparent carried by every Button in
        FormMap.Designer.cs: just the centred glyph, no button surface in any interaction state. The
        :pointerover / :pressed / :disabled template overrides suppress the Fluent hover / press /
        disabled fill that would otherwise box the glyph; :disabled also dims the glyph via Opacity to
        reproduce the greyed look WinForms applies to a disabled Button.Image (the gated controls render
        disabled at first show). Same technique as the sibling FormFieldDirView.

        CheckBox.imageToggle — reproduces the two WinForms `Appearance = Button` image check-boxes
        (cboxEnableLineDraw / cboxDrawMap): a flat image button that fills MediumAquamarine when checked
        (FlatAppearance.CheckedBackColor). This reuses the established imageToggle template from
        Views/Config/ConfigVehicleControl.axaml (a ContentPresenter root bound to Background /
        BorderBrush / BorderThickness / Padding via TemplateBinding) so per-instance border values flow
        through — cboxEnableLineDraw keeps its 1px Gray border (FlatAppearance.BorderColor = Gray),
        cboxDrawMap has none (FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0). :checked swaps the fill to MediumAquamarine
        and :disabled dims it, matching the flatImage gated look.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="CheckBox.imageToggle">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <ContentPresenter Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                      BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                      BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                      Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                      Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                      HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"
                                      VerticalContentAlignment="Stretch" />
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="CheckBox.imageToggle:checked">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="MediumAquamarine" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="CheckBox.imageToggle:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root layout reproduces the WinForms anchoring: the map surface fills the remaining space on the
        left ( gMapControl: Anchor Top|Bottom|Left|Right => the "*" column ) and the 241-wide command
        panel is pinned to the right ( tableLayoutPanel1: Anchor Top|Bottom|Right => the "Auto" column,
        fixed Width 241 ). Margin "3" + the map's 3px right margin reproduce the designer's 3px gutters.
    -->
    <Grid Margin="3" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">

        <!--
            mapPlaceholder — replaces the WinForms `gMapControl` (the removed map-imagery surface). A
            dark panel (fixed, deliberately NOT themed) carrying the centred graceful-degradation
            message. Light text on the dark fill ( #FFE6E6E6 on #FF2B2B2B ≈ 11.5:1, WCAG AAA ). The
            code-behind never needs to touch it beyond addressing it by name, so the message is static.
        -->
        <Border x:Name="mapPlaceholder"
                Grid.Column="0"
                Margin="0,0,3,0"
                Background="#FF2B2B2B">
            <TextBlock Text="Background imagery unavailable on this platform"
                       Foreground="#FFE6E6E6"
                       FontSize="22"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Margin="24" />
        </Border>

        <!--
            Right-hand command panel — reproduces the WinForms tableLayoutPanel1 (241 wide, anchored
            Top|Bottom|Right). 3 columns (43.57% / 19.64% / 36.79% of 241) and 10 rows (row 3 is the
            designer's fixed 37px row; the rest are the designer's percentages). Each control is placed
            in the SAME (column,row) cell — and with the SAME ColumnSpan — as FormMap.Designer.cs.
            Row 5 is the designer's empty spacer row.
        -->
        <Grid Grid.Column="1"
              Width="241"
              ColumnDefinitions="43.57*,19.64*,36.79*"
              RowDefinitions="11.12*,7.35*,12.38*,37,13.54*,11.12*,11.12*,11.12*,11.12*,11.12*">

            <!-- Row 0, Col 0 — cboxEnableLineDraw: enter "trace boundary on the map" mode. WinForms
                 (Appearance.Button) 83x72, image BoundaryOuter, 1px Gray border, MediumAquamarine when
                 checked. Imagery-dependent => disabled (gated). -->
            <CheckBox x:Name="cboxEnableLineDraw"
                      Classes="imageToggle"
                      Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0"
                      Width="83" Height="72"
                      BorderThickness="1"
                      IsEnabled="False"
                      HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Trace boundary on map">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/BoundaryOuter.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </CheckBox>

            <!-- Row 0, Col 2 — btnDeleteAll: delete the last field boundary / clear the traced line.
                 WinForms 61x59, image Trash. Imagery-/boundary-workflow control => disabled (gated). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnDeleteAll"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="2"
                    Width="61" Height="59"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Delete all">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Trash.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- Row 1, Col 0 — labelNewBoundary: "New Bnd" caption (Anchor Top, centred). 14.25pt -> 19.
                 Runtime: gStr.gsNewFromDefault + " " + gStr.gsBoundary. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelNewBoundary"
                       Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0"
                       Text="New Bnd"
                       FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" />

            <!-- Row 2, Col 0 — btnDeletePoint: remove the last traced point. WinForms 87x78, image
                 PointDelete. WinForms starts Enabled=false; imagery-dependent => disabled (gated). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnDeletePoint"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0"
                    Width="87" Height="78"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Delete last point">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/PointDelete.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- Row 2, Col 1 (span 2) — lblPoints: "Points: n" readout (Anchor Left, MiddleLeft).
                 14.25pt -> 19. Runtime updated by the code-behind timer. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblPoints"
                       Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                       Text="Points: 12"
                       FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Left"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- Row 3, Col 1 (span 2) — labelBoundary: "Boundary" caption (centred). 14.25pt -> 19.
                 This is the designer's fixed 37px row. Runtime: gStr.gsBoundary. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelBoundary"
                       Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                       Text="Boundary"
                       FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- Row 4, Col 0 — btnAddFence: commit the traced points as a new field boundary. WinForms
                 61x61, image AddNew. WinForms starts Enabled=false; imagery-dependent => disabled. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnAddFence"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="0"
                    Width="61" Height="61"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Add fence boundary">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/AddNew.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- Row 4, Col 1 (span 2) — lblBnds: boundary count readout (Anchor None, TopCenter).
                 15.75pt -> 21. Runtime updated by the code-behind timer. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblBnds"
                       Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                       Text="2"
                       FontSize="21" FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" />

            <!-- Row 6, Col 0 (span 3) — cboxDrawMap: capture the displayed imagery as the field
                 background. WinForms (Appearance.Button) 78x76, image MappingOff (toggles to MappingOn),
                 no border (BorderSize 0), MediumAquamarine when checked, Anchor Bottom. Imagery-dependent
                 => disabled (gated). -->
            <CheckBox x:Name="cboxDrawMap"
                      Classes="imageToggle"
                      Grid.Row="6" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                      Width="78" Height="76"
                      BorderThickness="0"
                      IsEnabled="False"
                      HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Use imagery as field background">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/MappingOff.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </CheckBox>

            <!-- Row 7, Col 0 (span 3) — labelBackground: "Background" section caption (Anchor Top,
                 centred). 15.75pt -> 21. Runtime: gStr.gsBackground. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelBackground"
                       Grid.Row="7" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Background"
                       FontSize="21" FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" />

            <!-- Row 8, Col 0 — btnZoomOut: zoom the map out. WinForms 64x63, image ZoomOut (52x52).
                 Imagery-dependent => disabled (gated). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnZoomOut"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="8" Grid.Column="0"
                    Width="64" Height="63"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Zoom out">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ZoomOut.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- Row 8, Col 2 — btnZoomIn: zoom the map in. WinForms 69x56, image ZoomOGL (52x52).
                 Imagery-dependent => disabled (gated). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnZoomIn"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="8" Grid.Column="2"
                    Width="69" Height="56"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Zoom in">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ZoomOGL.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- Row 9, Col 0 — btnGo: recentre the map on the current GPS position. WinForms 63x57,
                 image FlagGrn. Imagery-dependent => disabled (gated). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnGo"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="9" Grid.Column="0"
                    Width="63" Height="57"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Go to current position">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/FlagGrn.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- Row 9, Col 2 — btnExit: close the dialog. WinForms 61x63, image OK64. This is the ONLY
                 control that does not depend on imagery, so it stays ENABLED (the dialog can always be
                 closed). IsDefault routes Enter to it for keyboard operability. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnExit"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Grid.Row="9" Grid.Column="2"
                    Width="61" Height="63"
                    IsDefault="True"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Exit">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
